  "name": "Thai Satay Marinade",
  "text": "Thai Satay Marinade\n\nPrep time: 10 minutes\n\nCooking time: 0 minutes\n\nTotal time: 10 minutes\n\nYield: Makes enough marinade for 500g of beef or chicken.\n\nStatus: Successful\n\nIngredients\n\n1/4 cup chopped fresh lemongrass stalks,\n\n2 roughly chopped shallots,\n\n4 cloves garlic,\n\n1 fresh red chilli,\n\n1 chopped thumb-size piece galangal,\n\n1/2 tsp turmeric,\n\n2 tbsp ground coriander,\n\n2 tsp cumin,\n\n3 tbsp dark soy sauce,\n\n4 tbsp fish sauce,\n\n5 tbsp brown sugar,\n\n2 tbsp vegetable oil,\n\n3 cardamom pods.\n\nPreparation\n\n1. Place all marinade ingredients in a blender and whizz until smooth.\n\n2. Leave the meat in the marinade for 4-18 hours.",
